<section id="problem" class="bg-navy-900 py-20 text-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 text-center">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-300">The problem</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold leading-snug sm:text-4xl">
      "Who represents me?" is a simple question with a surprisingly shaky answer.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-blue-100">
      Most "find your representative" tools borrow their data from other websites — unofficial sources
      that quietly go out of date or break without warning. CivicDog's own WordPress plugin started out
      that way, and it was never something you could fully rely on.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-blue-100">
      Now CivicDog gets its information straight from{' '}
      <span class="font-semibold text-white">Congress's official record</span> and keeps it up to date
      automatically — so the answer you get is the right one.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
